{"In GroupPermissionsV2.canManage() (no-args), the permission check includes AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW alongside MANAGE, making it functionally identical to canView(). A user with only VIEW permission on groups can pass the manage check and create top-level groups via GroupsResource.addTopLevelGroup(), which is a privilege escalation security issue.": 0.982012152671814, "In GroupPermissionsV2.getGroupIdsWithViewPermission(), groupResource.getId() returns the authorization resource entity's internal primary key instead of the group model ID, which is stored as the resource name via resolveGroup(). This causes the returned set to contain wrong IDs that don't match any actual group, breaking user search filtering by group membership.": 0.8218433856964111, "Removing the short-circuiting canViewGlobal check causes canView(GroupModel) to be evaluated for every group in the stream, forcing a fine-grained authorization check per group for users without global admin roles, leading to an O(N) performance degradation (N+1 evaluation problem).": 0.734352707862854}